From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Droidloom <droidloom@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] frameworks/base: do not install ext in vendor-only builds

Droidloom reuses the exact ext.jar from its pinned official system image and
builds only a matching vendor partition.  Mark the local sparse-tree copy
uninstallable so Kati does not require a dex artifact for this unrelated
system module whose transitive source projects are deliberately absent.
---
 Android.bp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 1d3afb341f43..fcfd994e4df8 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -726,7 +726,7 @@ filegroup {
 // ============================================================
 java_library {
     name: "ext",
-    installable: true,
+    installable: false,
     sdk_version: "core_platform",
     static_libs: [
         "libphonenumber-platform",
-- 
2.51.0
